.\" Man page for dreame-valetudo. Debian policy expects one for anything in
.\" /usr/bin, and lintian flags its absence. The sibling whiskerless project
.\" ships one on the same terms.
.\"
.\" A repo invariant (tests/python/test_release_config.py) asserts every
.\" command the CLI dispatches appears here, so the two cannot drift silently.
.TH DREAME-VALETUDO 1 "2026-10-28" "dreame-valetudo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dreame-valetudo \- root a Dreame robot vacuum and install Valetudo on it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dreame-valetudo
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dreame-valetudo
is an idempotent runbook for rooting a supported Dreame, Mova or Xiaomi robot
vacuum over USB and replacing its cloud with Valetudo. Run with no command, it
asks for the model and the robot, then drives every phase in order, resuming
wherever it left off.
.PP
Phases that write to the robot are marked DESTRUCTIVE below.
.B recon
can capture a disaster\-recovery copy of the robot's flash into its working
directory, and
.B root
warns and asks before flashing without one. The robot's factory data goes into
the backups directory, which no command deletes.
.PP
.B dreame-valetudo help
lists the supported models.
.SH ROOTING COMMANDS
.TP
.B auto
Drive the whole chain explicitly. Identical to running with no command.
.TP
.B doctor
Set up and verify the toolchain this machine needs.
.TP
.B fetch
Download the stage1 package and the Valetudo binary, verified.
.TP
.B recon
Phase 1, NON\-DESTRUCTIVE: validate the USB connection and record the robot's
configuration.
.TP
.B image
Open the firmware builder and unpack the built image when it arrives.
.TP
.B root
Phase 2, DESTRUCTIVE: flash the rooted image, checking every step.
.TP
.B valetudo
Phase 3: explain how the Valetudo binary is pushed onto the robot.
.TP
.BR push " [\fIkey\fR]"
Phase 3: do it. Back up over SSH, push the binary and reboot.
.TP
.B ui
On the robot's access point: wait for Valetudo, then open its web UI.
.SH AFTER ROOTING
.TP
.B rekey
Authorize your SSH key on an already\-rooted robot, over USB.
.TP
.BR backup " [\fIkey\fR]"
Capture or refresh the factory data without changing the robot.
.TP
.BR update-valetudo " [\fIkey\fR]"
Verify and atomically update Valetudo on an adopted robot.
.TP
.B restore
DESTRUCTIVE: return this robot to its captured stock firmware.
.TP
.B diagnose
On the robot's access point: check why the UI is not up.
.TP
.B fix-impl
Pin the Valetudo implementation for the robot's model.
.TP
.B fix-did
Repair a negative factory deviceId.
.TP
.B fix-key
Restore the miio key some units keep only in secure storage.
.TP
.B fix-wifi
Help with a Wi\-Fi drop\-out after rooting.
.SH MANAGING ROBOTS
.TP
.B status
What is done and what is left, for every robot.
.TP
.B model
Correct the saved model before the robot is rooted.
.TP
.BI rename " old new"
Rename a robot. Its configuration identity is unchanged.
.TP
.BI forget " name"
Remove a robot's working directory, including its recon recovery dumps. Its
factory backups are kept.
.TP
.BR clean " [\fB\-\-all\fR]"
Delete the download cache; with
.BR \-\-all ,
staged firmware too. Recovery material is always kept.
.TP
.B migrate
Run the one\-time workspace migration now, rather than on the next start.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
.B sshkey
Show, or generate, the SSH public key the firmware builder asks for.
.TP
.B verify-form
Check this model's live firmware\-builder form against its recorded golden.
.TP
.B verify-forms
Check every fastboot model's live form. For CI and maintenance.
.TP
.BR bench " ..."
Run and record a hardware qualification campaign.
.TP
.B install-udev
Linux only, once, needs sudo: grant USB access without sudo.
.TP
.B uninstall
Find every copy of this tool and remove the ones you pick. The workspace and
its backups are never touched.
.TP
.B version
Print the version. Also
.B \-V
and
.BR \-\-version .
.TP
.B help
Print the usage, or with a command, that command's line. Also
.B \-h
and
.BR \-\-help .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/dreame-valetudo/work/
Per\-robot working state, including recon's disaster\-recovery flash dumps, the
download cache and staged firmware.
.TP
.I ~/dreame-valetudo/backups/
Each robot's factory data, kept when a robot is forgotten and when this tool is
uninstalled. Delete it only when you no longer need to restore any robot.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DREAME_MODEL
The model key, skipping the picker.
.TP
.B DREAME_ROBOT
The robot to act on, skipping the picker.
.TP
.B DREAME_WORK
A different working directory.
.TP
.B DREAME_BACKUPS
A different backups directory.
.TP
.B DREAME_SSHKEY
The SSH key to authorize on the robot.
.PP
The usage text lists the remaining overrides.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a deliberate abort at a confirmation.
.TP
.B 1
An error.
.TP
.B 2
Refused by a safety gate.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation and the supported\-model notes:
.UR https://github.com/SisyphusMD/dreame-valetudo
.UE
